# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# entrypoint.sh is COPYed straight into the Docker image, and the staging deploy
# builds that image from the working tree. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows
# checkout rewrites the shebang to "#!/bin/sh\r", so Linux looks for an
# interpreter named "/bin/sh\r" and the container dies with the misleading
# "exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory". The scripts/ helpers run
# under Git Bash, where CRLF is likewise a hazard.
*.sh text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
